The two command-line tools of google/woff2 (woff2_compress and woff2_decompress) and two files of its library that set and make the transforms of the encoder (woff2_enc.cc, transform.cc): the files that the install script builds in place of the upstream files of the same names.

Upstream:   https://github.com/google/woff2 (MIT; the text is ./LICENSE, copied from the pinned commit, SHA-256 d42a3e363d99da22b860ab760faa37dfa9781d74c9f3ed634d05109081616513)
Commit:     7b67e12355fe7da148db5c19d4261f0a498a9537 (2026-10-28), the commit scripts/install-woff2.sh fetches and checks by the SHA-256 of its archive

Copied files (upstream path -> path here) and what differs. `git log -p` on each file is the diff from upstream: the first commit holds the
upstream file as it is, each later commit is one change of ours.
  src/woff2_compress.cc    -> src/woff2_compress.cc    SHA-256 of the upstream file aa568299c90171eae75c639b00d9192e924ffe7b3e06b4c0a354c174e6b7945a
      Changes of ours, one commit each: an optional second argument, the Brotli quality from 0 to 11 (WOFF2Params::brotli_quality, 11 as the tool
      has it without), and a check of the input before the buffer of the output is allocated (a file that is shorter than the sfnt header or
      longer than 256 MiB, or a font of more than 4096 tables, is declined with exit status 1).
  src/woff2_decompress.cc  -> src/woff2_decompress.cc  SHA-256 of the upstream file 17fae33a2f625e4ee3592ee64f54683dea2b488de456403cd84e11e329d6915c
      Changes of ours, one commit each: the 48 bytes of the header are checked before the buffer of the output is allocated (a length field that
      is not the size of the file, no table or more than 4096 tables, a total size field above kDefaultMaxSize are declined with exit status 1),
      and the buffer starts at most 100 times the size of the input instead of at the size the header announces.
  src/woff2_enc.cc         -> src/woff2_enc.cc         SHA-256 of the upstream file c7fad4dcb577219d292296f471ba68818473ebd25f6f9127ad17b3bef71deb37
      Change of ours, in its own commit: TransformFontCollection also calls TransformHmtxTable (transform.cc, which the library has and the decoder
      reads back) for a font that is not part of a collection, so that the hmtx table is stored in the transformed form of section 5.4.
  src/transform.cc        -> src/transform.cc         SHA-256 of the upstream file 94dac0e7bc140d26483372964826429c6500a404432191541104fd78bd1cb87a
      Change of ours, in its own commit: the transform of the hmtx table compares the left side bearing of an empty glyph with zero, as section 5.4 asks,
      where it skipped the glyph and so stored a value that the decoder does not give back.

The rest of the libraries is not copied: the woff2 library (the other files of src/ and include/) and the Brotli library come from the archives of the
pinned commits (the Brotli commit is the one the woff2 tree names as its submodule). scripts/install-woff2.sh checks the digest of each archive,
puts these files over the files of the same name in the woff2 tree and builds with the make rules of that tree.
